course: dictionary
lesson: 291
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An amplifier is a machine that makes sounds louder. Guitarists plug into one, but the word can also mean any device that makes an electric signal stronger. The context tells you which meaning is in use.
explain: «An electric guitar has a solid body and is quiet until it is plugged into an amplifier.» The clue is quiet: the guitar needs something to make its sound loud enough to hear. So the amplifier must be the thing that makes it louder.
explain: «An acoustic guitar has a hollow body that makes it louder without electricity.» This sentence says the guitar gets loud with no machine at all, so the hollow body does the work that an amplifier does for an electric guitar.
explain: Musicians often shorten the word to «amp», as in «turn up the amp». Before you decide what a word means, check the subject you are reading about and the clues around it.
fact: An amplifier is a machine that makes sounds louder, especially from guitars, microphones and music players.
fact: In science, an amplifier is any device that makes an electric signal stronger.
fact: «Amplifier» can also mean something that makes a feeling or effect stronger.
fact: «Amp» is a short, informal way to say amplifier.
fact: In a music system, the amplifier's stronger signal goes to a speaker, which turns it back into louder sound.
exercise: «An electric guitar is quiet until it is plugged into an amplifier.» What does the amplifier do here? | It stops the music | It makes the guitar lighter | It tunes the strings | *It makes the sound louder
exercise: Guitarists say «turn up the amp». What does amp mean? | A small tent for camping | A type of guitar string | *A short word for amplifier | A kind of drum
exercise: «The loud music was an amplifier of the excitement in the crowd.» What does amplifier mean here? | A machine that makes sound louder | *Something that makes a feeling stronger | A kind of electric wire | A person who plays the drums
test: «An acoustic guitar has a hollow body that makes it louder without electricity.» Which word tells you no machine is needed? | *electricity | body | louder | hollow
test: In science, what is an amplifier? | A kind of battery that stores power | *Any device that makes an electric signal stronger | A light bulb that glows | A type of wire for carrying water
exam: In «plug into the amplifier», which meaning fits best? | *A machine that makes sounds louder | A quiet room for practice | A small hook for hanging clothes | A song played at a wedding
